      "writtenOn": "2026-04-01T18:30:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This now fetches all entries from LDAP unconditionally and relies on the @truncated decorator to slice the result in Python. For a directory with 100k+ entries and a list_limit of 1500, Keystone will pull all 100k entries over the wire only to discard most of them. The limit should still be pushed down to the LDAP layer -- conn.search_s() (or _paged_search_s) should accept a limit parameter and stop paginating once enough results have been collected.",
      "revId": "79c6ded05cee425938e664903f0035a1bf7a7b65",
